    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with a clear focus on exploiting favorable matchups against struggling starters. **Jose Caballero** (78.35) and **Corbin Carroll** (78.18) headline our production expectations, both benefiting significantly from favorable pitching matchups. **Jose Caballero** is particularly well-positioned; facing a left-handed starter with a 4.61 xERA, his 13% dynamic platoon boost makes him our highest-scoring asset despite batting seventh. Meanwhile, **Corbin Carroll** continues his resurgence against Aldegheri, where a juicy 5.41 xERA matchup and a prime spot in the three-hole create a high-ceiling environment. **James Wood** (70.07) also commands attention, as his elite .407 xwOBA and top-of-the-order status override the minor drag caused by a high-holding opposing pitcher, making him a cornerstone play for stolen base volume.\n\nOn the bench, the decision to sit **Dalton Rushing** (39.25) was a razor-thin call. Despite his potential, he fell just below our \"Zebras\" floor of 40.0 due to a L/L platoon disadvantage against McClanahan and a bottom-third batting order position. We are opting for the stability of **Kyle Karros** (48.61) in the utility spot, whose matchup against a more hittable 4.52 xERA pitcher provides a slightly higher confidence interval for points. Owners should monitor the status of **Gabriel Moreno** and **Austin Riley** closely; while both possess strong scores of 65.57 and 65.47 respectively, they are facing pitchers with higher xERAs, and any late-breaking lineup changes could impact their projected run-production upside. We are keeping **Trevor Story** and **Josh Naylor** stashed, while hoping the remainder of the active lineup can capitalize on these favorable 5x5 conditions to gain ground in the standings.",
